{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cfdpx8edz6RsgrEPWeZ2Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is well-contained and structurally sound:\n\n- **Right unit for the logic.** The E.164 transform lives entirely in `OwnerTelephone.normalize`, the existing dedicated telephone helper, mirroring the sibling `OwnerEmail`. The function step `ValidateNewOwner` stays thin — it calls the helper, throws on failure, and republishes the body. Nothing leaked into the function classes.\n\n- **Cohesive, not a catch-all.** `normalize` carries out a single well-defined responsibility (produce an E.164 string or `null`): strip separators, honor an existing `+`/country code, otherwise assume `+61` and drop a leading `0`, then bound the digit count. Each step belongs to that one transform; the method isn't accreting unrelated concerns, and the javadoc (including the idempotency note) documents the contract clearly.\n\n- **Duplicate detection handled additively.** `ValidateUniqueTelephone` needed no code change — comparing E.164 values falls out naturally from running after `ValidateNewOwner`, and only its doc comment was updated to say so. That's the minimal, idiomatic touch.\n\n- **Consistent propagation of the behavior change.** The entity `@Pattern`, the exception javadoc, the handler javadoc, and both validation-step javadocs were all updated in lockstep, so a maintainer reading any one of them sees the same E.164 story.\n\nOne minor asymmetry worth noting but not blocking: `OwnerEmail` splits `normalize` + `isValid`, whereas telephone folds validity into `normalize` (returns `null`). This is defensible — E.164 validity is a property of the assembled digits, so a clean normalize/validate split isn't natural here — and it reads fine in context."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12124,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12124},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2163ca9d-0740-47f1-a883-9d55e0ac2c42","uuid":"9e9c6841-6f25-49d6-bb93-d2900d97f2b6","timestamp":"2026-10-02T17:46:13.824Z","request_id":"req_011Cfdpx8Q1Xi2dKkNUgKjgC"}
